16.223.m:
It is a supreme mystery, O goddess, the most excellent of sacred fords.
Formerly in the Kṛta age, O goddess, it was remembered as Pretatīrtha;
but when the Kali age arrived, it became Gātrotsarga.

The ghosts said:
'We are ghosts, O illustrious one, who have come here from afar;
having heard of the holy, best of sacred fords, we cannot obtain entry.'
